Date:   Tue Nov 17 11:43:26 2026 -0800

    wordread boxmodel, fix round 1: joined examples are the merges our boxes really make
    
    A logistic P(our boxes merge a pair | geometry) is fitted to soft labels (the chance one training box holds both
    words, from the ink shares) over every pair of training words on a sheet, with no distance cut. The geometry is in
    the first word's frame: the gap along and across, the overlap as a share of the shorter extent and in heights, the
    angle and the height ratio. Joined examples are real pairs drawn in proportion to the fitted chance, cut as the
    union box our grouping would make at their real place on the page, with exact targets: count 2 or more, and
    boundary columns where the extents separate (none for a stack). A pair is drawn again when its box would touch a
    held area or a held word. Same-line gaps are kept only as the gaps.json record. The count-0 note covers Terra's
    misses.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
