    wordread boxmodel (Task 15): the learned box model of how many words a box holds and where they divide
    
    Examples (box_examples): each box cut by crops.box_cut (the reader crops' own margin) in ink, text chance and,
    when given, the word heads' core and tags; the count target the exact Poisson-binomial of each Terra word's
    share of its ink in the box; the boundary target per column the exact chance of lying between two consecutive
    held words; doubt weights optional (None: 1); joined neighbours from two real word crops at gaps drawn from the
    measured same-line gaps (soft next word on a line of text, no distance cut); raises on held-quarter or
    answered-block words and boxes. K measured. BoxNet: smaller MobileNetV3 blocks plus masked dilated 1-D context;
    fit_boxmodel in a GPU turn, seeded; box_logp for Task 9 (per crop, batch-independent). run_boxmodel.py measures
    counts.json and gaps.json and builds examples_<q>; its fit is Task 8's. No training run.
    
